ement-with-bangladesh/articleshow/134770879.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-stresses-constructive-and-people-centric-engagement-with-bangladesh/articleshow/134770879.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-07T22:28:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134770934,imgsize-41210.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A quick lunch, then a Jantar Mantar march: How Rahul-led opposition once again kept police guessing]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/a-quick-lunch-then-a-jantar-mantar-march-how-rahul-led-opposition-once-again-kept-police-guessing/articleshow/134770741.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134770741.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The episode was the latest example of a 'dhappa' style protest that Rahul Gandhi and the Congress have recently used. The latest episode began after Congress president Mallikarjun Kharge announced an INDIA bloc sit-in at Jantar Mantar following the lunch. "Today, we will hold a sit-in protest at Jantar Mantar. Until our demands are met, we will continue to stage such protests," Kharge announced.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/a-quick-lunch-then-a-jantar-mantar-march-how-rahul-led-opposition-once-again-kept-police-guessing/articleshow/134770741.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/a-quick-lunch-then-a-jantar-mantar-march-how-rahul-led-opposition-once-again-kept-police-guessing/articleshow/134770741.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-07T22:27:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134770891,imgsize-119524.cms"/></item><item><title><!